(DIR/port.patch), made against the pin + every patch before it (zzabi included: the name sorts last, as zzabi does).
Every edit was verified by re-parsing its file (no new error under int-conversion / incompatible-pointer): a file's own
re-declaration of a function states the definition's return type (a u8 / pointer / void read through the wrong one: the
host's rax holds garbage the DS's r0 does not), and an argument-less K&R call that is the first thing its caller does
passes the caller's own leading parameters (r0..r3 are still the caller's arguments there on the DS).
